[$in title:["Wiring"]]
[$in description:["Wire and Route parameter contracts, capability positions and channel boundaries."]]
[$in head:[language_theme_head]]

[navbar]
[sidebar]
init_docs_sidebar()!
[section, $md:
    # Wiring

    Wiring describes parameter contracts for binding identity and choice
    constructors. It does not create callbacks, subscriptions or a UI runtime.

    A Wire preserves binding identity. A Route captures choice-constructor
    arguments for later completion. Neither introduces callbacks, subscriptions
    or implicit event delivery. See @#wiring-introduction (Wiring reference)
    for the complete contracts.
]

